{"id": 11, "ok": true, "cmd": "range", "ucas": "range t64", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "range", "type": "int", "empty": false, "exhaustive": false, "points": 32803, "undefined_points": 0, "min": {"value": 0, "exact": "0"}, "max": {"value": 64, "exact": "64"}, "fits": "u7", "sound_bound": [0, 16776450], "proved_bound": {"min": 0, "min_exact": true, "min_steps": "t64 is nondecreasing in t, so take t = 0:\n      dd/2/dd = 0, since 0 <= dd/2 < dd for dd >= 1", "max": 64, "max_exact": true, "max_steps": "t64 is nondecreasing in t; where t <= dd, so take t = dd:\n      (64dd + dd/2)/dd = 64 + (dd/2)/dd = 64, since 0 <= dd/2 < dd for dd >= 1"}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "symbolic", "text": "monotonicity and exact algebra give bounds that the sample reaches"}, "files": [], "text": "range of t64 -> int:\n  0..64\n  fits in u7\n  sampled 32803 points (domain has 67652270100 points); not exhaustive\n  sound bound (intervals): 0..16776450\n  proved bound (monotonicity, exact algebra): 0..64\n  the sample reaches both ends: the range is exactly 0..64 (proved)\n    max: t64 is nondecreasing in t; where t <= dd, so take t = dd:\n      (64dd + dd/2)/dd = 64 + (dd/2)/dd = 64, since 0 <= dd/2 < dd for dd >= 1\n    min: t64 is nondecreasing in t, so take t = 0:\n      dd/2/dd = 0, since 0 <= dd/2 < dd for dd >= 1\n"}
